A||||2||V8Fiero||EGR question. Cars acting funny||||8||
Z||000000||V8Fiero||06-24-2001||04:04 PM||||Yesterday while I was working on replacing the engine on the GT, the wife jumped in the 86SE to go get us something to eat. Once she got back the car was sputtering and spitting black smoke out. If you touched the gas pedal it would want to stall. I let it sit for the rest of the day while I worked on the GT. I started it up around 9 or so in the evening and it idled really high. Around the 2k mark and wouldnt kick down. Shut it off and opened the trunk lid. I did notice alot of exhaust gases coming out of the EGR valve. Would a bad valve cause these simptons? Oh yea. I have had the 32 code also.<P>Scott||||reg||8
Z||000001||FieroJoe||06-24-2001||10:32 PM||||I assume this is probably a V6...<P>Anyways, since exhaust gasses were spewing out of the EGR valve, that needs to be replaced definatly.  Also, if the valve was spewing gases, the vacuum seals were probably shot too, and large vacuum leaks like that can cause your high idle.  Also check the EGR tube, if that hasnt been replaced yet.<P>I'm just speculating here, since I'm not too familiar with EGR systems, but if the EGR valve wasnt working, then the combustion chamber temperatures would be much higher than normal, and maybe all that extra heat was burning off a lot of built up carbon and thus all the black smoke in your exhuast.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000002||V8Fiero||06-24-2001||10:42 PM||||Yep! V6. I did push up the diaphram and the engine started to stumble. It is idling right now about 2k. Otherwise it seems to run fine. I will check the tube more carefully. Could a guy just replace the gaskets and not the whole unit? The diaphram seems to work fine.<P>Scott||||reg||1
